      "item_id": "fs-id1165043210088",
      "kind": "example",
      "title": "Example 4.49",
      "position": 7,
      "nearest_heading": "Other Iterative Processes",
      "prompt_text": "Finding a Limit for an Iterative Process Let $F (x) = \\frac{1}{2} x + 4$ and let $x_{0} = 0 .$ For all $n \\geq 1 ,$ let $x_{n} = F \\left(\\right. x_{n - 1} \\left.\\right) .$ Find the values $x_{1} , x_{2} , x_{3} , x_{4} , x_{5} .$ Make a conjecture about what happens to this list of numbers $x_{1} , x_{2} , x_{3} \\ldots , x_{n} ,\\ldots$ as $n \\to \\infty .$ If the list of numbers $x_{1} , x_{2} , x_{3} ,\\ldots$ approaches a finite number $x \\star ,$ then $x \\star$ satisfies $x \\star = F \\left(\\right. x \\star \\left.\\right) ,$ and $x \\star$ is called a fixed point of $F .$",
      "prompt_latex_bits": [
        "F (x) = \\frac{1}{2} x + 4",
        "x_{0} = 0 .",
        "n \\geq 1 ,",
        "x_{n} = F \\left(\\right. x_{n - 1} \\left.\\right) .",
        "x_{1} , x_{2} , x_{3} , x_{4} , x_{5} .",
        "x_{1} , x_{2} , x_{3} \\ldots , x_{n} ,\\ldots",
        "n \\to \\infty .",
        "x_{1} , x_{2} , x_{3} ,\\ldots",
        "x \\star ,",
        "x \\star",
        "x \\star = F \\left(\\right. x \\star \\left.\\right) ,",
        "x \\star",
        "F ."
      ],
      "has_solution": true,
      "source_anchor": "fs-id1165043210088",
      "notes": ""
    },
